                         "markdown":  "### SolutionsPT OT Cyber Suite\n- One file opens every tool from a home page with recent files, help, the licence and these notes. Each tool still ships on its own for contractors.\n- A rail down the left switches between the tools, keeps each one open with your work in it, and marks a tool with unsaved changes.\n- A file dropped anywhere in the suite, or chosen with Open a file on the home page, opens in the tool that reads it.\n\n### Report review\n- A new tool for peer review. The author sends a review pack from the assessment or risk tool. Each reviewer reads the report as the client will, comments on it and on the engagement behind it (with a severity and, where useful, suggested wording), works through a checklist and the automatic checks, gives a verdict and saves a small review file.\n- The author imports the review files and replies to or resolves each comment. Where the text can be changed in the tool, suggested wording is accepted in one click, and the change can be undone.\n- From round 2, each earlier comment shows where that text is now and what it says now, so fixes can be checked.\n- An optional note and needed-by date go with the pack. Approval offers to fill in the QA review by field.\n- A reviewer can reply on an earlier comment, see what a suggested rewording changes as they type it, and turn a checklist \"No\" into a comment. The list of sections shows where you are in the report.\n- The review tool stays quick on long reports and works from the keyboard: the report is one Tab stop, the arrow keys move through it, and a Keyboard button lists the keys.\n- A review only warns: the Issue check and the export dialog say when a report is not reviewed or has changed since approval, and nothing stops a Final export.\n- Inside the suite, Send for review can open the pack straight in the review tool, and the reviewer\u0027s file can be handed back.\n\n### Risk assessment tool\n- A Report page for both reports: rename, hide, reword or reorder sections, as in the assessment tool.\n- A QA review by field, printed in document control in both reports.\n- An unrated threat prints \"Not rated\" in the threat register.\n\n### Wording in reports\n- Internal wording (\"the tool\", \"placeholder\") removed from client reports, and a double full stop in the risk executive summary fixed.\n\nSaved project files from v0.5 and v0.5.1 open unchanged."
